{"created": "2026-10-05T15:24:25.041946+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-05T15:24:25.314802+00:00", "id": 23165916, "conceptrecid": "23165915", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23165916", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23165915", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23165916", "metadata": {"title": "Packing k\u00b2\u2212c unit squares: s(k\u00b2\u2212c) = k for all large k", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23165916", "publication_date": "2026-10-05", "description": "<p>Preprint, version 1.1. For every fixed c, s(k^2-c) = k for all sufficiently large integers k, where s(n) is the side of the smallest square containing n non-overlapping unit squares. Explicitly, every packing of N unit squares in [0,k]^2 that are pairwise disjoint as closed sets has k^2 - N &gt;= 0.033 log k for every integer k &gt;= 2 (0.027 log k without the computer-assisted Lemma 4.10). The programs, data and logs, including two independent coverage checks for Lemma 4.10, are in the companion software record https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23164301 and at https://github.com/squarepacker/k2-minus-c. Use of AI: developed with extensive assistance from Claude (Anthropic), including the proofs, the text, the programs and the computation for Lemma 4.10; the author takes full responsibility. Not peer reviewed.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ryu, Sungjoon", "affiliation": null}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23165736", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23165915"}}]}}, "title": "Packing k\u00b2\u2212c unit squares: s(k\u00b2\u2212c) = k for all large k", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23165916", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23165916", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/2316591